Subject: [PATCH] 4658 part 3: an introduction card goes to its request's own
 conversation

The tester's box 54617 (the founder's seat, 12 Oct): an incoming introduction
request was shown inside an unrelated goal's chat. Read on the rows: request
5717 had its own incoming_request conversation from 09:18Z; at 09:26Z a
scheduled check ran in the founder's old goal thread, and its pending card
for the request was written there. A card that names no goal stayed in the
run's thread (row 250.1), and an introduction card names a request, not a
goal.

An introduction card now goes to the reader's own conversation for that
request (threads.introduction_request_id, type incoming_request); with none,
or a failed read, it stays where it was. No new text.

